<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF stock rises on price optimism.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF stock rises on price optimism.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson CSF shares rose on Wednesday on the back of sentiment that the price Alcatel Alsthom or Lagardere offered for the group in its privatisation would be relatively high, traders said.</p>
<p>The share was up 4.7 francs at 157.2 francs at 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>Views of the price varied however, with some suggesting a figure of between 160 and 170 francs a share and others between 180 and 200 francs.</p>
<p>Several traders said the latter range was relatively high.</p>
<p>The government is carrying out the privatisation by trade sale and, according to the Le Figaro newspaper, is expected to reveal the name of the successful bidder on October 16.</p>
</text>
